;; Python's read level's divergences (bin/reap's [:python :read], queue 201 PY10; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built:
;; PY10"): the classes of repr/python's known files at that level, test/python/roundtrip-known.edn (the round trip's :lines
;; levels, PY2), lex-check-known.edn and parse-check-known.edn (the native reader, PY9), and beside it pyi's front end's
;; scope-known.edn and compile-known.edn (PY5a, empty), in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (C8's way: from the known
;; files' :classes). A case is "CORPUS FILE" (scope's and compile's "CHECK/CORPUS FILE"), its reason "known CLASS: the
;; class's text" (bin/reap's c-known reader). A class a known file gains is added here by hand, with its kind and decision.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :rejected
  :title "CPython rejects the file; the read is judged on its class and message"
  :kind :design
  :why "a deliberately bad file of Lib/test (an unknown or wrong encoding, a character no identifier takes): ast.parse rejects it, the read gives (python/error CLASS MSG ...) with CPython's class and message, nothing to print (survey §5.3)"
  :decided "PYS3 (a) (the user, 2026-11-03); PY2"
  :match [#"^known rejected:"]}
 {:id :code-lines
  :title ":lines: the forms and the ast equal, the code compiled from the print not (its positions)"
  :kind :design
  :why "CPython 3.14's code generation depends on the lines a node spans beyond what tools/pydump's code_digest normalizes (exception ranges, jumps, LOAD_FAST fusion); :lines carries no lines; the same files pass every level in :full (PY3)"
  :decided "queue 175's DECISION (a) (the user, 2026-11-03)"
  :match [#"^known code-lines:"]}
 {:id :charset
  :title "an encoding the runtime has no charset for (KOI8-R)"
  :kind :design
  :why "jrt's charsets are the root/English set of the locales decision of 2026-10-11: Lib/test's module_koi8_r.py cannot be decoded (the lexer) or written back (the print)"
  :decided "queue 176's DECISION (a) (the user, 2026-11-03)"
  :match [#"^known charset:"]}
 {:id :error-message
  :title "the native parser rejects what CPython rejects, with another message or position"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "PY9 (PY9c: pegen's second pass, the invalid_ rules, pegen_errors.c's messages)"
  :why "the native parser's first-pass failure is reported as \"invalid syntax\" at the last token read; CPython's error passes are PY9c's"
  :decided "PY9b's scope (the coordinator, queue 199)"
  :match [#"^known error-message:"]}
 {:id :helper-error
  :title "the helper (tools/pydump) itself fails on the file: the native reader is not judged on it"
  :kind :design
  :why "a mutant with a lone CR inserted on which pydump.py tree --full fails: no reference to judge the native reader against (the mutants are not counted by bin/reap, as C's)"
  :decided "PY9b, by rule"
  :match [#"^known helper-error:"]}
]
